---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import UpcomingTalks from '../components/UpcomingTalks';
import AgendaDialog from '../components/AgendaDialog';
import { loadTalks, todayKey } from '../lib/talks';
import { recentPublications } from '../lib/publications';

const talks = loadTalks();
const recent = recentPublications();
---

<Base>
  <div class="landing-hero" role="img" aria-label="Jae Yeon Kim presenting at the civic tech preconference"></div>

  <aside class="landing-sidebar">
    <img src="/bigger_than_headshot.jpg" alt="Jae Yeon Kim" class="landing-profile-image" />
    <h2>Jae Yeon Kim</h2>
    <p class="landing-title">Assistant Professor of Public Policy<br />University of North Carolina at&nbsp;Chapel&nbsp;Hill</p>
    <p class="landing-title">
      Founder and Director, <a href="https://jaeyk.github.io/pof-lab/">People, Organizations, Futures Lab (POF&nbsp;Lab)</a>
    </p>
    <p class="landing-links">
      <i class="bi bi-envelope"></i> <a href="mailto:jaekim@unc.edu">Email</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
      <i class="bi bi-file-earmark-text"></i> <a href="/CV_Jae_Yeon_Kim.pdf">CV</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
      <i class="bi bi-google"></i> <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=v2h903EAAAAJ&hl=en">Scholar</a>
    </p>
    <p class="landing-tagline"><strong>My research aims to make policy implementation work.</strong></p>

    <section class="landing-box" aria-labelledby="upcoming-talks-heading">
      <h3 id="upcoming-talks-heading">Upcoming Talks &amp; Events</h3>
      <UpcomingTalks client:load talks={talks} buildDate={todayKey()} />
      <p class="landing-box-link"><a href="/talks/talks.html">Full talks calendar</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="landing-box" aria-labelledby="new-publications-heading">
      <h3 id="new-publications-heading">New Publications &amp; Media</h3>
      <ol>
        {recent.map((p) => (
          <li>
            {p.url ? <a href={p.url}>{p.title}</a> : p.title}
            {p.meta && <span>{p.meta}</span>}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <p class="landing-box-link"><a href="/publications/pubs.html">All publications</a></p>
    </section>
  </aside>

  <p class="hello">Hello! I am Jae.</p>

  <p>
    I am an Assistant Professor of Public Policy at <a href="https://publicpolicy.unc.edu/person/jae-yeon-kim/">the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill</a>
    and the founder and director of the <a href="https://jaeyk.github.io/pof-lab/">People, Organizations, Futures Lab (POF Lab)</a>. I am also a fellow at the
    <a href="https://civicpowerlab.us/">Civic Power Lab</a> at the Harvard Kennedy School and a <a href="https://www.bettergovernmentlab.org/">Better Government Lab</a>
    Fellow at the University of Michigan's Ford School of Public Policy. In Spring 2027, I will be on research leave and visiting UC Berkeley's
    <a href="https://besi.berkeley.edu/">Berkeley Economy &amp; Society Initiative</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    Previously, I worked as a Senior Data Scientist at <a href="https://codeforamerica.org/">Code for America</a>, where I collaborated with the U.S. government to
    improve access to safety net programs. I also served as an Assistant Research Scientist at the SNF Agora Institute at Johns Hopkins University, where I
    co-developed <a href="https://snfagora.jhu.edu/our-work/research-projects/mapping-the-modern-agora/">the Mapping the Modern Agora Project.</a> I earned my Ph.D. in
    Political Science from the University of California, Berkeley.
  </p>

  <p>
    I am a policy scholar and public interest data scientist. Combining my experience as a data scientist in the U.S. public sector with my training as a social
    scientist, I study policy implementation, government capacity, and technological change. Specifically, my research examines how government can help people
    navigate bureaucracy, strengthen public trust, and buy and use technology, including but not limited to AI systems, effectively and responsibly. (If you want to
    see the connection between these areas, <AgendaDialog client:visible />.)
  </p>

  <p>
    I'm currently finishing a book manuscript (monograph) titled <a href="/book_projects/books.html"><em>Unseen and Uncounted</em></a>, which examines how the
    administrative challenges of identifying and categorizing non-Black minority communities gave rise to new racial group formations during the War on Poverty. My
    second book project, tentatively titled <em>Burdens, Profits, and People Power</em>, investigates how AI exacerbates existing inequalities through administrative
    burdens, what kinds of businesses profit from these hidden practices, and how people can build power, resist, and transform this unjust system.
  </p>

  <p>
    My research has appeared in leading journals across public policy and the social sciences. To produce research that directly informs policy and improves
    practice, I often collaborate with <a href="/community_building/partners.html">government, philanthropic, think tank, and nonprofit partners</a>. My research and
    expertise have helped U.S. state and local governments deliver public services, buy and use AI systems, and train government officials; foundations distribute
    grants for public benefit innovation and civic engagement; think tanks set agendas for responsible AI governance; and nonprofits develop their evaluation
    capacity.
  </p>

  <p>
    I am the recipient of the Sherman Family Emerging Scholar Award, The Korea Society (2026), the Paul Volcker Junior Scholar Research Grant Award in Public
    Administration (2025), the Emerging Scholar Award in Civic Engagement (2024), and the Best Dissertation Award in Urban and Local Politics (2022) from the American
    Political Science Association, as well as the Don T. Nakanishi Award for Distinguished Scholarship and Service in Asian Pacific American Politics (2020) from the
    Western Political Science Association.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout-note student-note">
    <div class="callout-header">For Prospective PhD and UNC Students</div>
    <div class="callout-body">
      <p>
        <strong>PhD Students</strong>: I will not be taking students in the coming cycle (starting in Fall 2027). If you are interested in working with me, please
        read my <a href="/essays/contacting_potential_advisors.html">advice for prospective PhD students</a>. If you then choose to email me, please explain (1) which
        of my work you have read, (2) why it is connected to your research agenda, and (3) how I can help you develop it. I look forward to working with
        self-motivated, intellectually curious students who approach their research with a healthy dose of skepticism, a big dose of imagination, and a relentless
        attention to detail.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>UNC graduate and undergraduate students</strong>: I cannot serve on your committee or advise on your honors thesis unless I know you well and there
        is a strong alignment between your topic and my research expertise. If you think you could benefit from my expertise, please reach out to me by email and
        schedule a time during <a href="/office_hour/office_hour.html">my office hours</a>. Also, if you are an undergraduate student interested in working with me on
        a research project, I encourage you to check out my <a href="https://jaeyk.github.io/pof-lab/">lab website</a>!
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="clear: both;"></div>
</Base>
